  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Anomalously warm low-level thicknesses and\ndewpoints beneath strong ridging aloft will continue to keep \ntemperatures well above normal with potential record breaking \nheat continuing today, with heat index values peaking at \n105-110 deg this afternoon for most of the area. Heat Advisory\ncontinues for most of the area, with highs in the 90s and\ndewpoints in the 70s. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A strong upper level trough will develop off \nthe U.S. East Coast over the weekend, and this will help drive a\nstrong cold front south through the Carolinas through tonight. \nThis plus increased forcing along the cold front and other \nlingering boundaries has supported an increased risk of deep \nconvection, and less limiting factors, compared to previous \ndays. PW's/TD's inc further and with lowering hts aloft, \ninstability will be very strong. 2.5kJ/kg were evident on this\nmorning's 12Z sounding and RAP is showing 4.5kJ/kg along the\nCrystal Coast ahead of the seabreeze, well above the avg max \nfor first week of September according to the KMHX sounding \nclimatology. If convective timing aligns with fropa/shortwave \npassage in the afternoon, a significant severe weather signal \nmay be met as this aligns with stout deep layer shear, possibly \nin excess of 35-45kt. Machine learning severe probs for damaging\nwind continue to tick up for parts of ENC. In addition to the \nsevere threat, will have to watch for potential flash flood \nthreat, as PWs surge to 2.25\" or higher, and with the expected \nnumerous convection, very heavy rain rates are possible with \ndeeper convection and lend to instances of flash flooding, \nespecially with potential for training of storms. Flood Advisory\nhas been issued for the severe warned storm that impacted \nHavelock and propagating Sward toward Bogue Banks with some \npockets of 5in/hr rain rates.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Behind the front, temperatures and humidity \nwill finally get knocked down closer to normal for early \nSeptember, with more comfortable conditions lasting into early \nnext week. Still some residual moisture lingering on Sunday and\nmay see some sct showers, but overall trend is for drier esp as\nwe begin the work week with pops less than 20% lasting through\nmid week. Highs in the mid 80s with lows in the 60s is fcst and\nis where our temps should be for the first half of September.",
